# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API connectivity
#
# Set this to the deployed ASP.NET Core API origin before building the
# frontend. Do not use localhost for a client deployment unless the API runs
# on the same client machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5064/api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public base URL encoded into animal QR codes (Phase 2B)
#
# A QR code printed for a field tag must open on a PHONE. A phone resolves
# "localhost" to itself, so a tag generated on the farm PC using
# http://localhost:3000 will never work in the paddock.
#
# Set this to the farm PC's LAN address, for example:
#     VITE_QR_BASE_URL=http://192.168.x.x:3000
#
# Leave it empty to fall back to whatever origin the browser is using. The QR
# card then shows a visible warning, because a localhost QR cannot be scanned
# from another device. It can also be overridden per-browser in the UI, which
# is stored under the localStorage key `dairy_farm_qr_base_url`.
#
# This value is PUBLIC. It is embedded in printed QR codes.
# NEVER put a password, JWT signing key, API key or OAuth token in any
# VITE_* variable - everything prefixed VITE_ is shipped to the browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_QR_BASE_URL=
